Track 2: "Will the Chrysalis Hold Our Weight?"
- Story & Context: Holed up in the sweltering loft of a dry-docked shrimp boat in Morro Bay, Mara Vane spent seventy-two continuous hours trying to tune her six-string bass to the severe tape drag of the time capsule's decaying B-side. Her fingertips split and bled over the heavy flatwound strings while salt crystals from her hair fell across the corroded vacuum tubes, filling the cramped cabin with the sweet, metallic scent of singed brine. Exhausted and weeping from sleep deprivation, she realized the warble on the tape wasn't an equipment error but a human heartbeat picked up by telemetry mics, crying into her telephone-receiver microphone as the band launched into a weightless, cavernous groove: "We built our chrysalis out of copper wire and rust, waiting for the sky to hatch."
