Track 3: Azimuth Instar
- Story & Context: Long after the original tape disintegrated into orange dust on a workbench in 2001, local legend claimed that playing the third movement's chromatic tremolo riff at Point Mugu during the autumn equinox would trigger swarms of ghost crabs to align themselves in neat geometric parabolas along the waterline. The myth culminated when three patrol officers reported hearing twang-drenched marine reverb washing out of their radio cruisers with no transmission source found, accompanied by the scent of ozone and drying kelp. The bootleg transcription remains an elusive underground holy grail, remembered solely for its haunting final guitar glissando that drops an octave into absolute silence beneath a whispered line: "Leave your wings in the sand, the tide is pulling into orbit."
